e Division II school offered Ole Miss fans attending its Oklahoma matchup free admission due to the kickoff date change.","published":"2026-11-14T22:28:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481529/central-oklahoma-troll-ole-miss-faa-decsion","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State WR Smith sets Big Ten record, states Heisman case","description":"Ohio State wide receiver Jeremiah Smith broke yet another record, eclipsing the Big Ten mark for career receiving yards while also making his Heisman Trophy case in Saturday's win over Northwestern.","published":"2026-11-14T23:15:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481134/ohio-state-jeremiah-smith-sets-big-ten-receiving-record","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4875126/horace-lockett","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horace_Lockett"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Horace Lockett","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horace_Lockett","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:20Z","intro":"Horace Lockett (born July 26, 2004) is an American college football defensive tackle for the UCF Knights. He previously played for the Georgia Tech Yellow Jackets.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at Georgia Tech in 2022, Lockett made three appearances. He saw more playing time in the 2023 season and tallied 25 tackles along with 2.5 tackles-for-loss (TFLs) and a forced fumble. However, a hand injury resulted in Lockett being kept out of every game during the 2024 season. The following year, he transferred to the UCF Knights. With UCF, Lockett won a starting role and posted 13 tackles, three TFLs, a sack and two pass breakups. However, a pectoral injury ended his season after four games. Lockett returned for a final season with the Knights in 2026."}]}}